       interesting to treat separately or together.  It’s possible to  specify
       what  subsets  are to be decoded, with a set of bits _s_e_l_e_c_t_i_o_n that are
       passed in an iinntt.

       This set of bits depend entirely on what kind of  provider‐side  object
       is  to  be decoded.  For example, those bits are assumed to be the same
       as  those  used  with  pprroovviiddeerr--kkeeyymmggmmtt(7)  (see   "Key   Objects"   in
       pprroovviiddeerr--kkeeyymmggmmtt(7))  when  the object is an asymmetric keypair - e.g.,
       OOSSSSLL__KKEEYYMMGGMMTT__SSEELLEECCTT__PPRRIIVVAATTEE__KKEEYY if the object to be decoded is supposed
