       When  a  provider‐native  object  is  created  by a decoder it would be
       unsuitable for direct use with a foreign provider. The export  function
       allows  for  exporting  the  object  into  that foreign provider if the
       foreign provider supports the type of the object and provides an import
       function.

       OOSSSSLL__FFUUNNCC__ddeeccooddeerr__eexxppoorrtt__oobbjjeecctt(()) should  export  the  object  of  size
       _o_b_j_r_e_f___s_z  referenced by _o_b_j_r_e_f as an OOSSSSLL__PPAARRAAMM(3) array and pass that
       into the _e_x_p_o_r_t___c_b as well as the given _e_x_p_o_r_t___c_b_a_r_g.

